%% RAINBOHz reference implementation - render and delivery pipeline
%% Referenced from: overview.md, section "Render and delivery pipeline"
%%
%% The message-bus hops are the current general idea, not a settled protocol.

sequenceDiagram
    participant client as playback-client / playback-plugin
    participant play as playback-server
    participant store as object-storage
    participant bus as message-bus
    participant comp as hzl-compiler
    participant engine as rendering-engine
    participant edb as engine-db

    client->>play: audio for a time range, with these labels
    play->>store: what exists for this source version?

    alt everything up to date
        store-->>play: objects for every shard
    else gap
        store-->>play: incomplete
        play->>bus: compile and render the required audio
        bus->>comp: compile
        comp->>comp: lower HzL to canonical-form
        comp->>bus: render
        bus->>engine: render (frame, labels, source version)
        engine->>edb: load canonical-form, transform to rendering model
        engine->>edb: read dirty flags and object references
        Note over engine,edb: delta determination reads the graph only,<br/>never object-storage
        engine->>engine: precompute segments, phase compensation
        engine->>engine: render frames
        engine->>store: write multi-channel WAV objects
        engine->>bus: rendering complete
        bus->>play: rendering complete
        play->>store: read objects for every shard
        store-->>play: objects
    end

    play->>play: sum the shards
    play-->>client: summed audio
